(From the perspective of Seller's Advocate, the transaction architecture constructed under the Agreement and Plan of) Tj
T* (Merger dated October 5, 2026, exhibits robust structural integrity and comprehensive risk insulation across its control) Tj
T* (topology, financing structure, and regulatory execution framework. First, regarding the $2.873B equity financing and) Tj
T* ($3.15B debt package, the transaction possesses zero financing conditionality: the definitive merger agreement expressly) Tj
T* (stipulates that the closing is not conditioned on Parent's receipt of financing, and Parent and Merger Sub remain legally) Tj
T* (obligated to consummate the merger regardless of syndication status. To eliminate execution vulnerability, the Target is) Tj
T* (designated an express third-party beneficiary under the executed Equity Commitment Letters delivered by Clayton,) Tj
T* (Dubilier & Rice Fund XII, L.P. and McKesson Corporation \(aggregate commitments of $2,873,295,853\), conferring direct) Tj
T* (legal standing on the Target to compel specific performance against the Guarantors to fund their equity commitments) Tj
T* (upon the satisfaction or waiver of closing conditions. Second, if a buyer financing default or uncured breach were to) Tj
T* (occur, the structure provides asymmetric monetary deterrents: Parent is obligated to pay a $291,927,951 Parent) Tj
T* (Termination Fee \(approximately 5.0% of equity value, twice the size of the Company Termination Fee of $145,963,976\),) Tj
T* (backed by binding, several Limited Guarantees from CD&R Fund XII and McKesson Corporation, plus an enforcement) Tj
T* (expense recovery capped at $7.5M. Third, with respect to the co-investment by strategic participant McKesson) Tj
T* (Corporation and vertical healthcare regulatory considerations, the merger agreement rigorously allocates regulatory) Tj
T* (closing risk. The parties are bound by a 'reasonable best efforts' standard to obtain governmental and antitrust clearances) Tj
T* (under the Hart-Scott-Rodino \(HSR\) Antitrust Improvements Act of 1976, while Parent is subject to a heightened, unilateral) Tj
T* ('best efforts' legal standard to obtain specified healthcare consents, waivers, orders, and State Boards of Pharmacy) Tj
T* (authorizations. The drop-dead Outside Date extends to October 5, 2027 at 11:59 p.m. Eastern Time, providing a) Tj
T* (substantial 12-month runway to navigate regulatory clearances. Finally, the post-closing control topology preserves) Tj
T* (operational continuity by retaining Option Care Health as a stand-alone operating entity led by incumbent management) Tj
T* (\(CEO John C. Rademacher and CFO Meenal A. Sethna\), while delivering immediate, fully certain cash consideration of) Tj
T* ($32.05 per share to Target stockholders, insulating them entirely from therapeutic gross margin headwinds, IRA CMS) Tj
T* (pricing adjustments, and vendor concentration exposures.) Tj
