(The transaction's architectural integrity and control topology remain fully insulated against buyer-side critiques concerning) Tj
T* (equity syndicate apportionment, several liability, and regulatory clearance. First, regarding financing conditionality and) Tj
T* (syndication mechanics, the Merger Agreement establishes as an express contractual fact that closing is not conditioned) Tj
T* (on Parent's receipt of financing. The Target's closing risk is fully protected by executed Equity Commitment Letters) Tj
T* (delivered by Clayton, Dubilier & Rice Fund XII, L.P. and McKesson Corporation totaling $2,873,295,853, alongside a fully) Tj
T* (committed debt financing package of $3.15 billion in term facilities and $500.0 million in revolving facilities. The definitive) Tj
T* (agreement confers express third-party beneficiary status directly upon Option Care Health, establishing unambiguous) Tj
T* (legal standing to compel specific performance against the Guarantors to fund their equity commitments upon the) Tj
T* (satisfaction or waiver of closing conditions. While the executed guarantees for the $291,927,951 Parent Termination Fee) Tj
T* (\(and enforcement expenses capped at $7.5 million\) are entered into severally and not jointly, the total committed capital) Tj
T* (of $6,023,295,853 substantially exceeds the total transaction uses of $6,023,295,853 \(including cash consideration of) Tj
T* (~$4.80B, refinancing of the $672.9M First Lien Term Loan balance, discharge of the $500.0M Senior Notes, and) Tj
T* (estimated fees/expenses of ~$124.8M\), precluding liquidity shortfalls. Second, the adversary's critique regarding vertical) Tj
T* (integration frictions involving strategic co-investor McKesson Corporation \(against Target's historical supplier) Tj
T* (concentration of 68% across four vendors\) is contractually neutralized by the asymmetric regulatory risk allocation: while) Tj
T* (antitrust clearance under the HSR Act requires 'reasonable best efforts', Parent is bound by a heightened, unilateral 'best) Tj
T* (efforts' legal obligation to obtain all required healthcare consents, waivers, orders, and State Boards of Pharmacy) Tj
T* (authorizations across Target's network of 86 full-service pharmacies and 187 ambulatory infusion suites. Third, the) Tj
T* (Outside Termination Date is set for October 5, 2027 at 11:59 p.m. Eastern Time, providing an extensive 12-month) Tj
T* (timeline to clear state-level licensing and federal regulatory reviews without triggering drop-dead vulnerabilities. Finally,) Tj
T* (the post-closing control structure preserves operational continuity under existing executive leadership while completely) Tj
T* (immunizing Target stockholders from chronic therapy margin compression, IRA CMS pricing headwinds, and ongoing) Tj
T* (BioScrip unclaimed property audit liabilities through full cash-out consideration at $32.05 per share.) Tj
