(The Seller asserts that the $2,873,295,853 equity commitment package and $3.15B debt commitment render the) Tj
T* (transaction execution fully insulated. However, an analysis of the control topology, syndicate governance, and regulatory) Tj
T* (mechanics reveals critical structural exposures. First, the equity commitment of $2,873,295,853 and the Parent) Tj
T* (Termination Fee \($291,927,951\) backed by Clayton, Dubilier & Rice Fund XII, L.P. and McKesson Corporation are strictly) Tj
T* ('several and not joint.' Public disclosures \(Form 8-K Item 1.01\) do not specify the exact individual percentage or dollar) Tj
T* (contribution between CD&R Fund XII and McKesson. While Option Care Health is designated an express third-party) Tj
T* (beneficiary entitled to seek specific performance of the equity commitments, Delaware law enforces the contractual terms) Tj
T* (as drafted: a failure or default by one equity guarantor does not obligate the other to step in or cure the shortfall. Second,) Tj
T* (the user directive notes McKesson is providing a $1.4B minority co-investment. This indicates an approximate 48.7%) Tj
T* (equity contribution by McKesson \($1,400,000,000 / $2,873,295,853\), placing McKesson near joint-control governance) Tj
T* (thresholds under corporate and regulatory frameworks. If CD&R and McKesson have entered into unfiled side letters,) Tj
T* (voting agreements, or governance pacts concerning Parent \(Onyx Bidco LLC\) or post-closing board appointments, such) Tj
T* (arrangements may trigger Section 13\(d\) group formation or regulatory concert-action scrutiny under healthcare licensing) Tj
T* (and antitrust review. Third, regulatory risk allocation establishes an asymmetric standard: HSR clearance requires only) Tj
T* ('reasonable best efforts', whereas Parent is bound by 'best efforts' solely for specified healthcare/pharmacy licensing.) Tj
T* (McKesson is a primary wholesale pharmaceutical distributor. Target disclosures establish that Option Care Health) Tj
T* (purchased 68% of its pharmaceutical and medical supplies from four vendors in 2025, and 57% from three vendors in H1) Tj
T* (2026. A substantial minority equity stake \(~48.7%\) held by McKesson directly integrates the upstream wholesale supply) Tj
T* (chain with Target's downstream provider network \(86 pharmacies and 187 ambulatory infusion suites across 43 states\).) Tj
T* (Because HSR is governed solely by 'reasonable best efforts', Parent and McKesson are not contractually compelled) Tj
T* (under the standard to agree to structural remedies or supply unbundling conditions that exceed reasonable bounds,) Tj
T* (creating an execution impasse prior to the October 5, 2027 drop-dead Termination Date.) Tj
