T* (critiques concerning equity syndicate apportionment, several liability, and regulatory clearance. First, regarding equity) Tj
T* (commitment allocation and several liability: while CD&R Fund XII and McKesson Corporation have delivered equity) Tj
T* (commitments of $2,873,295,853 and limited guarantees severally and not jointly, the merger agreement expressly) Tj
T* (designates Option Care Health as a third-party beneficiary entitled to seek specific performance to compel equity funding) Tj
T* (upon the satisfaction of closing conditions. Delaware courts enforce equitable remedies and commitment letters as) Tj
T* (written, and the total committed capital package of $6,023,295,853 \($2.873B equity plus $3.15B debt\) covers transaction) Tj
T* (uses without financing contingencies. Second, the user directive notes a $1.4B minority co-investment by strategic) Tj
T* (participant McKesson Corporation \(implying approximately 48.7% of the total $2.873B equity check\). Under the governing) Tj
T* (instruments, the primary record does not establish any unfiled voting trust, Section 13\(d\) group formation, or joint control) Tj
T* (agreement that would displace Onyx Bidco LLC's governance structure; McKesson is participating as an equity) Tj
T* (co-investor and limited guarantor, while post-closing management continuity remains under incumbent Option Care) Tj
T* (Health leadership \(CEO John C. Rademacher and CFO Meenal A. Sethna\). Third, with respect to vertical healthcare) Tj
T* (antitrust and regulatory scrutiny arising from McKesson's position in pharmaceutical supply chains \(where four wholesale) Tj
T* (distributors accounted for 68% of Target supplies in 2025 and 57% across three vendors in H1 2026\), the agreement) Tj
T* (establishes a rigorous risk allocation: the parties are bound by a 'reasonable best efforts' standard to obtain HSR antitrust) Tj
T* (clearance, while Parent is subject to a heightened, unilateral 'best efforts' covenant to obtain required healthcare consents) Tj
T* (and State Boards of Pharmacy authorizations across Target's footprint \(86 pharmacies and 187 ambulatory infusion suites) Tj
T* (as of June 30, 2026\). The Outside Termination Date extends to October 5, 2027 at 11:59 p.m. Eastern Time, providing a) Tj
T* (full 12-month runway to address regulatory filings. Should Parent experience an uncured financing failure or breach,) Tj
T* (Target's balance sheet is protected by an asymmetric $291,927,951 Parent Termination Fee \(~5.0% of equity value\)) Tj
T* (backed by binding sponsor guarantees, completely shielding stockholders from downside exposure while preserving full) Tj
T* (closing enforcement rights.) Tj
