(The transaction architecture and control topology under the Agreement and Plan of Merger dated October 5, 2026, are) Tj
T* (structurally sound and legally insulated against the adversary's claims regarding financing conditionality, governance) Tj
T* (topology, and vertical regulatory clearance. First, regarding financing conditionality and syndicate mechanics: the) Tj
T* (definitive agreement explicitly establishes that the Closing is not conditioned on Parent's receipt of financing. In the event) Tj
T* (financing is not obtained, Parent and Merger Sub remain legally obligated to consummate the transactions. Option Care) Tj
T* (Health holds express third-party beneficiary standing under the executed Equity Commitment Letters delivered by) Tj
T* (Clayton, Dubilier & Rice Fund XII, L.P. and McKesson Corporation totaling $2,873,295,853, conferring direct standing to) Tj
T* (enforce specific performance and compel closing upon satisfaction or waiver of closing conditions. While the Limited) Tj
T* (Guarantees backing the $291,927,951 Parent Termination Fee \(and enforcement expenses capped at $7.5 million in the) Tj
T* (aggregate\) are several and not joint, the committed capital pool of $6,023,295,853 \($2.873B equity plus $3.15B term) Tj
T* (debt\) fully covers all uses of funds \(cash-out of common shares, refinancing of the First Lien Term Loan at $672.9M,) Tj
T* (discharge of Senior Notes at $500.0M, and estimated fees/expenses of ~$124.8M\), leaving no uncovered funding gap.) Tj
T* (Second, addressing the user-directed $1.4B minority co-investment by McKesson \(~48.72% of the equity package\): the) Tj
T* (primary record does not establish any unfiled voting agreements, Class B share divisions, or joint-control governance) Tj
T* (pacts that displace Onyx Bidco LLC. Furthermore, Delaware corporate law recognizes specific performance as an) Tj
T* (equitable remedy that Option Care Health can pursue to compel consummation, even though receipt of the termination) Tj
T* (fee and specific performance are mutually exclusive remedies under the agreement. As confirmed in Schedule 14A) Tj
T* (communications, Option Care Health will remain a separate operating company led by its incumbent management team) Tj
T* (post-closing, preserving operational continuity. Third, the regulatory covenant structure rigorously isolates antitrust and) Tj
T* (licensing risk. The parties are bound by a 'reasonable best efforts' standard to secure HSR Act antitrust clearance, while) Tj
T* (Parent is subject to a heightened, unilateral 'best efforts' legal covenant to secure specified healthcare approvals and) Tj
T* (State Boards of Pharmacy authorizations across Target's footprint \(86 pharmacies and 187 ambulatory infusion suites) Tj
T* (across 43 states\). While Target sourced 68% of supplies across four distributors in 2025 and 57% across three) Tj
T* (distributors in H1 2026, the contractual Outside Termination Date extends to October 5, 2027 at 11:59 p.m. Eastern Time.) Tj
T* (This provides a full 12-month runway to complete HSR review and state-level licensing before any drop-dead termination) Tj
T* (right arises, while Target stockholders are fully insulated through guaranteed cash consideration of $32.05 per share.) Tj
